{"id": "x0702", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most helpful tool for investigating the life cycle of a monarch butterfly would be B, a magnifying glass. This allows you to closely observe the different stages such as eggs, caterpillars, chrysalises, and adult butterflies with detail, which is essential for accurate study. While options like A, C, and D may have uses in other contexts, they are not directly suited for observing the intricate details of the butterfly's life cycle.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0710", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 17, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The jar most likely contained oxygen gas. When the teacher opened it, the gas spread out and filled the room because gas es naturally diffuse to fill any available space. Cloth fibers or salt water would not spread as easily, and snowflakes would melt quickly in a classroom setting. So oxygen gas is the best answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0718", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, wind vane and an emometer. Wind chill depends on both the wind speed and the temperature. A wind vane measures wind direction, while an emometer measures wind speed. These two together provide the data needed to calculate wind chill.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0726", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's think about this carefully. When you mix salt with water, the water is what dissolves the salt. In a solution, the substance that dissolve s something else is called the solvent, and the thing being dissolve d is the sol ute. So here, water is doing the dissolving, which means it is the solvent, and salt is the so lute. That makes sense because we add salt to water to make a salty solution. Now looking at the options: A says salt is the solvent, which is wrong. B says salt is the solute and water is the solvent—that matches our logic. C says salt is the solvent and water is the solution, but that doesn't fit because water is part of the solution. D say s salt is the solution, which isn' t right either. So the best answer is B: salt is the so lute and water is the solvent.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 46, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0734", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 23, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the correct answer is C, all of the fossil s show similar structures to that of the modern horse. When we talk about evolution, what we're looking for are changes in structure over time. If a series of fossils shows gradual changes in bone structure or other features that resemble the modern horse but with differences, it suggests an evolutionary link. The other options don' t really prove evolution. For example, if they were found in the same layers as horse fossils, that just means they lived around the same time. And if they were completely identical, there's no change to suggest evolution. Also, location doesn't matter as much as the structural changes seen across the fossils. So C is the best choice because it shows evidence of change over time, which is key to proving evolution.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 42, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0742", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, nervous. Ne rvous cells send signals to muscle fibers that tell them when to contract or relax, which allows us to control our movements.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0750", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 29, "onset_chunk": 28, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "B, by giving the comb an electrical charge is correct. When Greta runs the comb through her hair, it pick s up static electricity from friction with her hair strand s. This gives the comb a slight electrical charge. The stream of water nearby also carries tiny charges on its surface. When the charged comb gets close to the water, the water molecules respond to that electric field. They are polar molecule s, meaning they have positive and negative ends. The opposite charges in the water are attracted to the comb, causing the stream to bend toward the comb even though the comb isn't touching it. So the static electricity created by running the comb through hair causes the water to be pulled in its direction.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 42, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0758", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Oak tree decline is linked to several factors, including pathogen ic fungi, insect de foliation, soil chemical stress, and microorgan ism activity. The question asks which factor is an abiotic condition. Abiotic factors are non-l iving elements, like climate or soil conditions. Path ogenic fungi and in sect defoliation involve living organisms, so they are biotic. Microorganism activity also involves living micro bes, making it bi otic as well. That leaves soil chemical stress, which refers to changes in the soil' s chemistry, such as nutrient levels or pH. This is a non-living environmental condition that affects trees. Therefore, the correct answer is C, soil chemical stress.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0766", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 36, "onset_chunk": 35, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, during an El Niño event, upwelling in the equatorial Pacific Ocean decreases. That means less cold, nutrient rich water is brought to the surface. The surface water temperature rises as a result.So, let ’s look at each option one by one. A: Decrease in release of carbon dioxide to the atmosphere. Well, remember that upwelling water has dissolved carbon di oxide. When up welling stops, there is less mixing and less CO2 is released from the ocean to the air. But wait— warmer water actually hold s less CO 2. However, since biological activity might slow down because of fewer nutrients, the overall effect is usually a slight decrease or no significant change in CO2 release. But this is not the most direct consequence we’re looking for.B: Increase in photosyn thesis by algae in surface waters. Al gae need nu trients like nitrates and iron that come from up welling. If up welling declines, nutrient supply drops, so photosynthesis likely decreases, not increases. So B is unlikely.C: Increase in dissolved oxygen in surface waters. When upwell ing stops, warm surface water holds less oxygen, and with less al gal growth due to nutrient shortage, there is less oxygen production through photos ynthesis. So dissolved oxygen would probably decrease, not increase. So C is wrong.D : Decrease in precipitation", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0774", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Petroleum is a key raw material in the production of plastic soda bottles, so option A is correct.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0782", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A small laundry room with shelves above the washing machine is primarily an example of B, using storage space efficiently. These shelf s make use of vertical space that would otherwise be empty, allowing for additional items to be stored without taking up more floor area.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0790", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Recycl ing paper helps save trees that would otherwise be cut down for new paper. Since fewer trees are removed, the habitat s of animals living in those forest areas are less likely to be destroyed. So the correct answer is D: it preserves animal habitats from being destroyed.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "x0798", "pool": "know-arc", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, breaking down waste s. Ly sosomes are like the stomachs of cells. They contain enzyme s that break down waste materials and old cell parts. So when food is digested, lysosomes help process the leftovers by breaking them into smaller pieces.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
